        "text": "b12x provides optional CUDA kernels for NVIDIA SM120 and SM121 GPUs (RTX Pro 6000/5000, RTX 5090, DGX Spark GB10), installed with pip install vllm[b12x]. b12x linear kernels participate in automatic selection after established optimized backends and before emulation; select them explicitly with --linear-backend b12x and --moe-backend b12x. Only pass --moe-backend b12x for a compatible NVFP4 or MXFP4 MoE model. b12x uses MXFP8 activations by default for MXFP4 MoE and the checkpoint's activation format for NVFP4 MoE; set VLLM_B12X_MOE_FP4_FORCE_A16=1 to force BF16 activations for either FP4 weight format. Linear supports per-tensor FP8, 128x128 block FP8, MXFP8, NVFP4 and MXFP4. The b12x MoE backend does not support expert parallelism, expert maps, EXL3, or NF3.",
